<LegalShell
  title="Cookies"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="How Infinite Weblinks uses cookies and similar technologies. Today the site is deliberately light: no advertising or tracking cookies are set by default."
  path="/cookies"
  lastUpdated="13 July 2026"
>
  <p>Cookies are small files a website can store in your browser. This page explains which ones this site uses and why. We keep it short because, today, the site uses very few.</p>

  <h2>What we use now</h2>
  <p>This is a static website. It does not set advertising or cross-site tracking cookies, and it does not profile you as you move between pages. Any cookies present are limited to what the browser or a form processor needs to work when you submit an enquiry.</p>

  <h2>Forms</h2>
  <p>When you send a form, the third-party processor that delivers your message to us may use a cookie or similar technology to protect against spam and abuse. This is used to make the form work securely, not to track you around the web.</p>

  <h2>If this changes</h2>
  <p>If we later add analytics, video, maps or other embedded tools that set cookies, we will list them here and, where required, ask for your consent before they load. We would rather add them honestly than switch them on quietly.</p>

  <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>You can clear or block cookies in your browser settings at any time. Because the site does not depend on tracking cookies, blocking them will not stop you reading anything here.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>For anything about cookies or your data, see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy page</a> or <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.</p>
</LegalShell>
